## Retro

configureIde is closer to the bar than most specs but pays a Strategy bloat
cost from research-grade rationale on Zed's extension API. The right home
for that material is a brain research note; the spec commits to the decision
("Zed = config patch, VS Code = bundled extension") and references the
research. Trim Strategy ≤80 words per decision.
